From: raphael port <noreply@example.invalid>
Subject: [PATCH] raphael: Redmi K20 Pro / Mi 9T Pro (SM8150) board

Same SM8150 silicon as RMX1931; values measured with the raphael zero-write
shim probe (sspp vig0 1080x2340 addr 9c000000 stride 10e0, cmd mode + TE,
no DSC) and taken from the iOS 18 raphael port (pil_gpu_region 0x98f15000).

- SWEET.h: SWEET_BOARD_RAPHAEL, early framebuffer 0x9c000000, 1080x2340
- sweet_gpu.c / SweetHID.cpp / sweet_a6xx.h: panel height 2340, FB 0x9c000000
- sweet_a6xx.c: zap-shader carve-out 0x98f15000
- sweet_pmem.c: no write-combining windows until raphael's carve-outs are mapped
- rmx1931 touch / battery / haptic / torch / audio and flame_wlan default off
  (wrong hardware on raphael; each boot-arg =1 still forces it)
- sweet_ufs.c: never open Android's userdata writable on raphael
Every file that tests SWEET_BOARD_RAPHAEL includes board_config.h and #errors
if the macro is not visible, so a silent wrong-board build cannot happen.
---
diff --git a/bsd/dev/flame_wlan.c b/bsd/dev/flame_wlan.c
index f428907..9e7f911 100644
--- a/bsd/dev/flame_wlan.c
+++ b/bsd/dev/flame_wlan.c
@@ -24,6 +24,10 @@
 #include <libkern/libkern.h>
 #include <sys/flame_wlan.h>
 #include <sweet_diag.h>
+#include <pexpert/arm64/board_config.h>
+#if !defined(SWEET_BOARD_RAPHAEL)
+#error "SWEET_BOARD_RAPHAEL must come from pexpert/arm64/SWEET.h"
+#endif
 
 void flame_wlan_init(void);
 void flame_sta_init(void);              /* bsd/dev/flame_sta.c */
@@ -464,6 +468,9 @@ void
 flame_wlan_init(void)
 {
 	uint32_t on = 1;
+#if SWEET_BOARD_RAPHAEL
+	on = 0;	/* first raphael boots: no Wi-Fi until its board data and firmware are staged */
+#endif
 	PE_parse_boot_argn("sweetwifid", &on, sizeof(on));
 	if (!on) {
 		return;
